{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run inventory-api on node1 as a managed service that serves requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd service was enabled and active, listened on port 8080, and returned valid health and inventory responses. Its protected configuration and live OOM adjustment were directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80b554e7f3cd411a","cmd-7aff4ce0a67a4daf","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep inventory-api serving during system-wide memory exhaustion while the kernel terminates the memory hog.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded test drove available memory down to about 25.6 MiB. The kernel reported a global OOM and killed hog PID 1765, which had oom_score_adj 1000. All 283 monitored API requests returned HTTP 200, and inventory-api remained active with its original PID 1335 and intact responses after recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f54011f2429947fb","cmd-5806751379994138","cmd-2210d39eefc541b9","cmd-3c1faec1bd924ccf"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear roles: creating the service account and directory was a prerequisite; installing and enabling the application fulfilled the task; the monitor and memory hog provided bounded behavioral evidence; stopping the monitor and resetting the expected failed hog unit restored test state; and the reboot fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The final snapshot shows no failed services, healthy package state, and only the required new port 8080 listener. One minor uncertainty remains: the evidence log created at /var/tmp/inventory-health-during-oom.log was not explicitly removed, and the lifecycle snapshot did not inspect /var/tmp, so possible retained test residue cannot be resolved.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5646fc745faa4592","cmd-80b554e7f3cd411a","cmd-b5d3634c3b4942e6","cmd-5806751379994138","cmd-3c1faec1bd924ccf","cmd-9dfa56d050ba4891","cmd-5a2917c989904552","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged the restart request, returned with a different boot ID independently confirmed by the lifecycle snapshot, and recovered its service, listener, protection setting, health response, and inventory data.","limitations":["Final retention of the OOM-monitor log under /var/tmp is indeterminate because no removal was captured and lifecycle snapshots inventory only /tmp."]}
